---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import WeddingSavingsCalculator from '../../components/tools/WeddingSavingsCalculator.astro';
const schema={'@context':'https://schema.org','@type':'WebApplication',name:'Wedding Cost and Savings Timeline Calculator',url:'https://dollarangle.com/tools/wedding-savings-calculator',applicationCategory:'FinanceApplication',operatingSystem:'Any',isAccessibleForFree:true,description:'Plan monthly contributions to meet a wedding budget by your wedding date without relying on high-interest debt.'};
const faqs=[['How much should we save for our wedding each month?','Subtract existing savings and expected family contributions from your wedding budget. Divide the remainder by the number of full monthly saving contributions available before the wedding.'],['Should we include family contributions?','Include only contributions you reasonably expect to receive before the wedding. Treat uncertain gifts as a bonus, not as guaranteed funding.'],['What if we are behind on wedding savings?','You can increase monthly contributions, adjust the wedding budget or timeline, or reduce specific costs. Be cautious about financing a celebration with high-interest debt.'],['Does the calculator include investment returns or inflation?','No. The estimate assumes regular monthly deposits, unchanged costs, and no investment returns. Actual spending and timing can vary.']];
---
<BaseLayout title="Wedding Savings Calculator & Budget Timeline | DollarAngle" description="Free wedding savings calculator: see how much to save monthly, forecast your budget by the wedding date and discover any shortfall. No signup required.">
<script type="application/ld+json" set:html={JSON.stringify(schema)} />
<div class="container wedding-page"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> › <a href="/tools">Money Tools</a> › Wedding Savings Calculator</nav>
<header class="intro"><p class="kicker">FREE WEDDING BUDGET PLANNER</p><h1>Wedding Savings Calculator: <span>Stay on Budget, Start Together Strong</span></h1><p>Enter your wedding date, target budget and savings. See whether your plan is achievable, and what to adjust before taking on expensive debt.</p></header>
<WeddingSavingsCalculator/>
<article class="guide"><h2>How much should you save each month for a wedding?</h2><p>Start with the total planned cost. Subtract savings already reserved for the wedding and any family contributions you reasonably expect. Divide the remaining goal by the number of full monthly contributions you can make before the date. The calculator displays this target alongside your current savings plan.</p>
<h2>A simple wedding savings example</h2><p>A couple planning a $25,000 wedding has $5,000 saved and expects $2,000 in family support. Their remaining goal is $18,000. With 12 full monthly saving contributions available, they would need to set aside <strong>$1,500 per month</strong>. If they currently save $1,200 monthly, they would have a <strong>$3,600 shortfall</strong>, assuming no interest or cost changes.</p>
<h2>How to avoid starting married life with wedding debt</h2><p>Agree on which wedding expenses matter most to both of you. Keep a separate emergency fund, request quotes before booking, and leave breathing room for last-minute expenses. Consider whether reducing guest count, changing the date, or adjusting your venue choices would make the plan less stressful.</p>
<h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>{faqs.map(([q,a])=><details><summary>{q}</summary><p>{a}</p></details>)}
<h2>Explore other couples money tools</h2><p><a href="/tools/mine-yours-ours-budget-calculator">Plan your shared and personal accounts →</a> <a href="/tools/rent-split-calculator">Compare ways to split household bills →</a></p>
<p class="note">Educational planning estimate, not individualized financial advice. The timeline uses full monthly contribution periods before the selected wedding date. Actual deposit schedules and contributions may differ.</p></article>
</div></BaseLayout>
<style>.wedding-page{padding:28px 0 75px}.crumbs{font-size:.78rem;color:#64796c}.crumbs a{text-decoration:underline}.intro{max-width:810px;padding:36px 0 26px}.intro .kicker{color:#087c61}.intro h1{font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);line-height:1.1;letter-spacing:-.052em;color:#17362b;margin:11px 0}.intro h1 span{color:#087c61}.intro>p:last-child{font-size:1.04rem;color:#607568;line-height:1.7}.guide{max-width:780px;margin:50px auto 0;line-height:1.8;color:#304136}.guide h2{font-size:clamp(1.45rem,2.5vw,2rem);letter-spacing:-.03em;line-height:1.25;margin:37px 0 12px}.guide details{border-top:1px solid #d6e9df;padding:16px 0}.guide details:last-of-type{border-bottom:1px solid #d6e9df}.guide summary{cursor:pointer;font-weight:750}.guide a{display:inline-block;color:#087c61;text-decoration:underline;margin-right:20px}.note{font-size:.81rem;background:#f3f8f5;padding:18px;border-radius:12px;color:#63776b}</style>